      "writtenOn": "2018-12-10T23:35:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There might be multiple components need the injection. So there would be a list of them. Therefore it could be either:\n\n\u003cinjection package jar component\u003e\n\u003cinjection package jar component\u003e\n\nor:\n\u003cinjection package jar\u003e\n    \u003ccomponent\u003e\n    \u003ccomponent\u003e\n\nPerhaps the latter follows a more commonly used pattern, and could avoid package/jar mismatch for listed components. Additionally, it\u0027s more common to see wrapping a list of xml \u003celement\u003e inside a \u003celements\u003e. So the pattern ends up with:\n\u003cinjection\u003e\n    \u003ccomponents\u003e\n        \u003ccomponent\u003e\n        \u003ccomponent\u003e",
